**Given:**

Speed at the time of going from A to B = 9 km/h

Speed at the time of going from B to A = 15 km/h

**Concept used:**

Time = Distance/Speed

**Calculation:**

Let the distance of A to B be x km

Ratio of Time from B to A and from A to B = (frac{x)/(15)}{(x)/(9)}

⇒ {(x)/(15)}times{(9)/(x)}

⇒ {(9)/(15)}

⇒ {(3)/(5)}

So, ratio = 3 : 5

**∴ Required ratio is 3 : 5.**
